# === Vendored upstream packages (third_party/) ===
# These are the packages as delivered by upstream, kept on disk for reference. They are NOT
# committed, for one measured reason: `godot/addons/axie_mixer_3d*` already holds the copy the
# game actually loads, and on 2026-09-19 `diff -rq` showed the two are byte-for-byte identical.
# Committing both would put ~391MB of duplicate data into history permanently — and history is
# the one thing that is painful to take back.
#
# The single exception is the golden fixture below: four gates read it
# (t_axie_gene_preview, t_axie_api, qa_vault_preview_capture, qa_vault_screen_capture), so a
# fresh clone without it has four failing tests and no obvious reason why. It is 9.9 KB.
# NOTE ON THE PATTERN SHAPE: a bare `third_party/` would make git skip the directory entirely,
# and a `!` exception under an excluded directory is never even looked at. Each level has to be
# opened with `dir/*` and then re-included, which is why this is five lines instead of one.
third_party/*
!third_party/godot-axie-mixer-3d-main/
third_party/godot-axie-mixer-3d-main/*
!third_party/godot-axie-mixer-3d-main/tests/
third_party/godot-axie-mixer-3d-main/tests/*
!third_party/godot-axie-mixer-3d-main/tests/goldens/
production/leaderboard/verdicts/

